  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...A stalled front continues to bisect the area\nthis evening. Convection beginning to wane with loss of heating\nthis evening, mainly relegated to the SW forecast area. 12z/29 \nKMHX sounding has PW near record values for the day at 2.27\" and\ncould continue to see locally heavy rainfall where storms train.\nThe front will dissipate overnight with convection primarily \nalong the sea breeze Sunday afternoon. Guidance showing a bit \nmore instability tomorrow with MLCAPE peaking around 1500J/Kg \nbut also shows descent coverage of mid and high clouds \nthroughout the day as moist SW flow persists aloft, so maximum \ninstability may not be realized keeping convection more isolated\nin nature. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Shower and thunderstorm coverage wanes next \nweek as upper ridging builds into the region from the west. \nCannot completely rule out an isolated shower or storm through \nthe period along sea and sound breezes although activity will \nlikely be short-lived. The main story will be the building heat \nwith highs expected to climb into the 90s early next week and \npeaking in the mid to upper 90s as we move into the middle of \nthe week. Heat headlines may be needed as early as Wednesday \nwith forecast heat indices climbing above 105, especially along \nthe coast and inland counties along and south of US70.",
